Hello, our name is Customertimes, but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries.

**About this job:**

***You will be***
a Service Cloud platform specialist
***who takes***
over consumer product support for a global technology company, moving cases, knowledge, and support channels from a legacy system to Salesforce.
***You will work***
inside the client's engineering team with their Pune and US colleagues, and alongside a wider program that brings AI agents into the CRM.

**Location:Pune**

**How you'll make an impact:**

* Design and build Service Cloud features: case management, Omni-Channel routing, Service Console, Knowledge, Entitlements and Milestones, Email-to-Case and Web-to-Case,
  ***and***
  messaging or chat channels;
* Write Apex, Lightning Web Components, and Flows, with test classes that meet the client's coverage and quality standards;
* Build and maintain integrations with REST and SOAP APIs, platform events, and middleware;
* Support data migration from the legacy support system: mapping, loads, validation,
  ***and***
  cutover;
* Work in a source-driven release process (Git, SFDX, CI/CD) and with QA on every release;
* Join design reviews and estimate work with the client's tech leads.

**What makes you a great fit:**

* 5+ years of hands-on Salesforce development: Apex, LWC, Flows,
  ***and***
  SOQL;
* 3+ years on Service Cloud, including case management and Omni-Channel;
* Integration experience: REST APIs, named credentials,
  ***and***
  external services;
* Source control and CI/CD on Salesforce (Git, SFDX; AutoRabit, Copado, or Gearset);
* Salesforce Platform Developer I certification;
* Clear written and spoken English
  ***and comfort working***
  with US teams.

Join a dynamic, multidisciplinary team and take part in exciting projects.

SERVO-ROBOT develops and manufactures 3D vision systems for industrial robotics, and our innovations in this cutting-edge sector are recognized and used on all five continents. Our teams of engineers and technicians are experts who constantly tackle world-class challenges. From our headquarters in Saint-Bruno-de-Montarville, Quebec, we export most of our products to North America, Asia, and Europe through our network of subsidiaries and partners.

Our Indian subsidiary **SERVO ROBOT Pvt. Ltd.** located in Hyderabad, India is looking for a **Welding Engineer** with a hands-on welding experience.

**Position: Robotic Welding Engineer**

*Job Description:*

- Support customers in the use of SERVO-ROBOT vision systems;

- Contribute to AI-based welding model development and introduction of new technologies and products;

- Analyze customer applications using robotics and engineering expertise;

- Conduct application tests and take part in real world projects;

*Requirements:*

*-* Diploma in Welding Engineering/ Welding Technician or equivalent;

*-* Knowledge of manufacturing industry, and welding robots;

*-* IWE – International Welding Engineer certification is an asset;

*-* Availability to travel to customer’s sites;

**Qualified candidates may send their resumes to:**

humanresources@servorobot.com

Work Location: In person
